{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-87d75248-024d-456f-8ca1-3113ae110a33","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d8853f5273019f3","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-vbx4q__o/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E001.md","content":"# Investigate plugin workspace-resolution coupling to tracking-store initialization\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves whether the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins`\n`kubernetes-auth` plugin's workspace resolution and workspace store\ninitialization depend on tracking store or model registry store\ninitialization. The artifacts-only server context deliberately leaves those\nstores uninitialized, so the answer determines whether the plugin works\nas-is in that context (verification only) or requires refactoring to factor\nworkspace resolution into an independent initialization path. The outcome\nselects between two conditional downstream work plans.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Trace the plugin's workspace provider / workspace store initialization path,\n  including its registration through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry\n  point group and loading via the workspace store registry.\n- Identify every initialization dependency the plugin's workspace resolution\n  has on tracking store, model registry store, or full tracking-server\n  initialization.\n- If coupling exists: produce a scoped refactor plan (modules and files to\n  change, the approach for an independent initialization path, effort\n  estimate) that preserves the plugin's existing interface.\n- If no coupling exists: produce verification evidence that workspace\n  resolution initializes and resolves in a server context without tracking\n  stores.\n- Record the bounded outcome decision: outcome A (no coupling — verification\n  only) or outcome B (coupled — refactor required).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A findings document that traces the workspace-resolution initialization path\n  with concrete code references and states, as a pass/fail determination,\n  whether it depends on tracking store or model registry store availability.\n- If coupled: a refactor plan naming the affected modules and the proposed\n  independent initialization path, sufficient to scope and schedule the\n  refactoring work.\n- If not coupled: verification evidence (test or harness output) demonstrating\n  workspace resolution initializing without tracking stores.\n- The bounded outcome is recorded so the matching conditional work plan can be\n  selected.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 (P1): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the\n  artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization — this\n  investigation determines the scope of that work.\n- Informs HLR-2 (P0): end-to-end workspace-validated artifact serving depends\n  on the plugin resolving workspaces in the artifacts-only context; the\n  investigation and its downstream work therefore inherit P0.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":88441,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8865428d5e28a0d8","agent_id":"a654abfb6cba3ce32","session_id":"c475d54c-6029-4a26-8892-bfb5b0182313","uuid":"4e1e4bb9-98b9-4a37-88e1-4cdc1d7a50cf","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:29:58.546Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
