{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f8396570-026c-44d9-ba69-7f473252dc88","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6e87dc958d96f4c","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-vbx4q__o/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E002.md","content":"# Workspace-aware artifacts-only serving in the MLflow server\n\n## Description\n\nMake the MLflow tracking server's `--artifacts-only` mode composable with the\nexisting `--enable-workspaces` flag so that the artifacts-only server\ninitializes only the workspace provider needed to validate artifact requests\nagainst tenant boundaries. No new server flag is introduced: the\nworkspace-aware behavior emerges from combining existing flags, per the Staff\nEngineer input. Tracking stores and model registry stores stay uninitialized\nand non-artifact API endpoints remain disabled. The design is fail-closed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Flag composition: allow `--artifacts-only` and `--enable-workspaces` to be\n  set together; when both are set, require an explicit `--workspace-store-uri`\n  (the server fails to start with a clear error if it is missing).\n- Initialization: initialize only the workspace provider needed to validate\n  artifact requests; keep tracking and model registry stores uninitialized and\n  non-artifact API endpoints disabled in this mode.\n- Artifact request validation: for each artifact request, resolve the artifact\n  path to its parent experiment (artifacts are stored under\n  experiment-scoped paths such as `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`), look\n  up the experiment's workspace assignment via the workspace store, and\n  delegate authorization to the existing auth plugin infrastructure. Requests\n  failing workspace validation receive HTTP 403. No new authorization\n  mechanism or Kubernetes API mechanics are prescribed — the existing plugin\n  infrastructure is reused.\n- Fail-closed behavior: when workspace-aware mode is active but the workspace\n  store is unreachable, deny artifact requests rather than serving them\n  without validation.\n- Backwards compatibility: `--artifacts-only` without `--enable-workspaces`\n  retains current behavior (no workspace validation); each flag used\n  individually preserves current behavior.\n- Scope the path-to-experiment resolution to the S3 artifact store (the\n  standard configuration) where paths follow the well-defined structure;\n  document limitations for non-standard artifact roots.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The server starts successfully with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces\n  --workspace-store-uri kubernetes://`, and non-artifact API endpoints remain\n  disabled in this mode.\n- The server fails to start with a clear error when `--enable-workspaces` is\n  set without `--workspace-store-uri`.\n- A user who is a member of workspace A requesting an artifact belonging to an\n  experiment in workspace A receives HTTP 200 with the correct artifact\n  content.\n- A user who is a member of workspace A but not workspace B requesting an\n  artifact belonging to an experiment in workspace B receives HTTP 403 with an\n  error message indicating insufficient workspace permissions.\n- With the workspace-aware artifacts-only server running and the workspace\n  store (Kubernetes API) unreachable, artifact requests are denied\n  (fail-closed), measured by an HTTP 503 response indicating workspace\n  validation is unavailable.\n- With `--artifacts-only` set without `--enable-workspaces`, any authenticated\n  user's artifact request is served without workspace validation (current\n  behavior preserved).\n- Each flag used individually (artifacts-only alone; workspaces alone on the\n  full tracking server) preserves current behavior — no existing API\n  contracts, CLI arguments, or configuration keys change meaning.\n- Workspace validation delegates to the existing auth plugin infrastructure;\n  no parallel authorization path is introduced.\n- Tests cover multi-tenant workspace scenarios, backwards compatibility,\n  single-tenant regression, and fail-closed edge cases for the artifact\n  serving path, including integration with the workspace provider running in\n  the artifacts-only context.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): `--artifacts-only` composable with `--enable-workspaces` and\n  `--workspace-store-uri`.\n- HLR-2 (P0): artifact requests validated against workspace membership;\n  non-members denied with HTTP 403 (server-side validation logic).\n- HLR-3 (P0): fail-closed behavior when the workspace store is unreachable.\n- HLR-4 (P0): single-tenant deployments and configurations without\n  `--enable-workspaces` retain current behavior (server-side share).\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Artifact path resolution may not map straightforwardly to experiment IDs in\n  all storage backends or custom artifact roots; initial implementation is\n  scoped to the S3 artifact store and limitations are documented.\n- The strategy's architecture review prerequisite is pending human review and\n  covers this epic's design.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":89137,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8865428d5e28a0d8","agent_id":"a654abfb6cba3ce32","session_id":"c475d54c-6029-4a26-8892-bfb5b0182313","uuid":"45b77a64-75c7-4ac0-b00e-9733419ceea3","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:30:21.461Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
