{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b6114f03-92fb-4108-959e-ed0ea16b451e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-876d63447b070cd2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-vbx4q__o/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E003.md","content":"# Operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance\n\n## Description\n\nExtend the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow\ninstance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute,\nforming a split-server topology: the main tracking deployment handles\nexperiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry, while the\ndedicated artifacts-only instance handles artifact serving with workspace\nvalidation. This is a topology change in the operator's Helm-in-operator\nrendering, not a single configuration toggle.\n\n## Scope\n\n- New Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and\n  HTTPRoute, rendered through the operator's existing embedded-chart,\n  server-side-apply pattern.\n- A CR configuration surface that enables the split-server artifact serving\n  topology (exact field naming is an implementation decision for the team).\n- Propagation of workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`,\n  `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only\n  instance using the same configuration mechanisms already used for the main\n  tracking deployment.\n- Conditional creation of the artifacts-only instance's Gateway API\n  HTTPRoute based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's\n  existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n- kube-rbac-proxy sidecar deployed on the artifacts-only instance identically\n  to the main tracking deployment (authentication layer unchanged).\n- Operator validation that rejects configurations enabling split-server\n  artifact serving where the artifacts-only instance would lack the workspace\n  flags (misconfiguration could let artifact requests bypass workspace\n  validation).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, the operator\n  reconciles the CR and creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment,\n  Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment, measured\n  by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the correct flag\n  combinations.\n- The artifacts-only Deployment runs with `--artifacts-only\n  --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name\n  kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`, measured by inspecting the container\n  command in the rendered Deployment spec.\n- The rendered flag combination is verified against the flag combination the\n  workspace-aware artifacts-only server supports, and end-to-end artifact\n  serving with workspace validation is verified against a server image\n  carrying that capability (coordination point with the server-side work —\n  not a start-order dependency).\n- The operator rejects CRs that enable split-server artifact serving without\n  the workspace configuration, with a clear validation error.\n- CRs without split-server artifact serving configured reconcile exactly as\n  before — no new resources are created and existing resources are unchanged\n  (single-tenant and non-workspace deployments are unaffected).\n- The artifacts-only HTTPRoute is created only when the Gateway API CRD is\n  discovered at runtime, consistent with the operator's existing conditional\n  pattern.\n- The chart change adds new templates without structural changes to the chart\n  architecture; if structural changes turn out to be required, the epic is\n  re-split (see the decomposition summary's Health Warnings).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-5 (P1): MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as\n  a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute.\n- HLR-4 (P0, constraining acceptance criterion): configurations without\n  `--enable-workspaces` retain current behavior — the operator's share is a\n  no-change constraint on the opt-in topology, not P0-enabling work.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- A split-server topology adds operational surface (two Deployments, two\n  Services, two HTTPRoutes); misconfiguration could let artifact requests\n  bypass workspace validation. Mitigated by operator-level validation of the\n  workspace flag combination.\n- The strategy's architecture review and ODH/RHOAI build onboarding\n  prerequisites are pending human review and cover this epic's design.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":90275,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8865428d5e28a0d8","agent_id":"a654abfb6cba3ce32","session_id":"c475d54c-6029-4a26-8892-bfb5b0182313","uuid":"f99dba09-99a2-47c7-8cc4-5d7a1f25f042","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:30:49.047Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
