{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-4e888e9f-696d-459f-bcf9-6909aec6ea27","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-82b8cb5ed595528b","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-vbx4q__o/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E004.md","content":"# Decide the artifact traffic routing mechanism for the split-server topology\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation decides how the MLflow operator should configure artifact\ntraffic routing from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated\nartifacts-only instance, and whether the tracking server needs a\nconfiguration change to delegate artifact operations. The answer determines\nwhich downstream routing work exists: gateway-level routing only, or\ntracking-server delegation requiring both operator configuration and\nserver-side support. The outcome selects between two bounded conditional\nwork plans.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Evaluate routing artifact traffic to the dedicated instance at the\n  gateway/HTTPRoute level (path-based routing on the artifacts-only\n  instance's own Service and HTTPRoute, with no tracking server change).\n- Evaluate routing via tracking-server delegation (the main tracking\n  deployment configured to delegate artifact operations to the dedicated\n  instance, requiring server-side configuration support).\n- Analyze the tracking server's existing artifact proxy configuration\n  surface and the operator's existing routing/rendering patterns to determine\n  feasibility of each option.\n- Assess the security implication either way: no routing path may allow\n  artifact requests to bypass workspace validation.\n- Record the bounded outcome decision: outcome A (gateway-level routing\n  suffices — operator work only) or outcome B (tracking-server delegation\n  required — operator plus server-side configuration work).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A documented recommendation identifying the routing mechanism, with a\n  feasibility analysis grounded in the operator's rendering/routing code and\n  the tracking server's artifact proxy configuration surface.\n- An explicit determination of whether the tracking server requires a\n  configuration change to delegate artifact operations, with the\n  configuration surface it would use if so.\n- An analysis confirming the selected mechanism cannot route artifact\n  requests around workspace validation.\n- The bounded outcome is recorded so the matching conditional work plan can\n  be selected.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the\n  dedicated artifacts-only instance — this investigation determines the\n  mechanism and scope of that work.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":91271,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8865428d5e28a0d8","agent_id":"a654abfb6cba3ce32","session_id":"c475d54c-6029-4a26-8892-bfb5b0182313","uuid":"d8caffcd-da58-4bc2-9bac-4e4033531952","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:31:08.075Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
