ther than serving on stale\n  authorization.\n- Tests cover cache expiry, invalidation, and the fail-closed interaction.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Supports the Performance NFR for the P0 artifact-serving HLRs (HLR-1\n  through HLR-3); implements the strategy's risk mitigation for per-request\n  workspace resolution overhead. Not an HLR itself — its necessity is decided\n  by the latency measurement and PM/Engineering threshold decision.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":92445,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8865428d5e28a0d8","agent_id":"a654abfb6cba3ce32","session_id":"c475d54c-6029-4a26-8892-bfb5b0182313","uuid":"26789156-69bd-43cd-be11-72fa19522dfc","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:31:41.345Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
