{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-afffe8f97d9075cd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n3\ttitle: Investigate plugin workspace-resolution coupling to tracking-store initialization\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigate plugin workspace-resolution coupling to tracking-store initialization\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves whether the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins`\n30\t`kubernetes-auth` plugin's workspace resolution and workspace store\n31\tinitialization depend on tracking store or model registry store\n32\tinitialization. The artifacts-only server context deliberately leaves those\n33\tstores uninitialized, so the answer determines whether the plugin works\n34\tas-is in that context (verification only) or requires refactoring to factor\n35\tworkspace resolution into an independent initialization path. The outcome\n36\tselects between two conditional downstream work plans.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Trace the plugin's workspace provider / workspace store initialization path,\n41\t  including its registration through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry\n42\t  point group and loading via the workspace store registry.\n43\t- Identify every initialization dependency the plugin's workspace resolution\n44\t  has on tracking store, model registry store, or full tracking-server\n45\t  initialization.\n46\t- If coupling exists: produce a scoped refactor plan (modules and files to\n47\t  change, the approach for an independent initialization path, effort\n48\t  estimate) that preserves the plugin's existing interface.\n49\t- If no coupling exists: produce verification evidence that workspace\n50\t  resolution initializes and resolves in a server context without tracking\n51\t  stores.\n52\t- Record the bounded outcome decision: outcome A (no coupling — verification\n53\t  only) or outcome B (coupled — refactor required).\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- A findings document that traces the workspace-resolution initialization path\n58\t  with concrete code references and states, as a pass/fail determination,\n59\t  whether it depends on tracking store or model registry store availability.\n60\t- If coupled: a refactor plan naming the affected modules and the proposed\n61\t  independent initialization path, sufficient to scope and schedule the\n62\t  refactoring work.\n63\t- If not coupled: verification evidence (test or harness output) demonstrating\n64\t  workspace resolution initializing without tracking stores.\n65\t- The bounded outcome is recorded so the matching conditional work plan can be\n66\t  selected.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-7 (P1): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the\n71\t  artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization — this\n72\t  investigation determines the scope of that work.\n73\t- Informs HLR-2 (P0): end-to-end workspace-validated artifact serving depends\n74\t  on the plugin resolving workspaces in the artifacts-only context; the\n75\t  investigation and its downstream work therefore inherit P0.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bca13937492c95c2","agent_id":"a4b202be07365c067","session_id":"c475d54c-6029-4a26-8892-bfb5b0182313","uuid":"06cc79aa-68a7-4f40-bab7-a116f9a09315","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:39:09.543Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-afffe8f97d9075cd","permission_decision":{"de