{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a101cc3d4d2009c3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n3\ttitle: Operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: -1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tExtend the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow\n34\tinstance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute,\n35\tforming a split-server topology: the main tracking deployment handles\n36\texperiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry, while the\n37\tdedicated artifacts-only instance handles artifact serving with workspace\n38\tvalidation. This is a topology change in the operator's Helm-in-operator\n39\trendering, not a single configuration toggle.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- New Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and\n44\t  HTTPRoute, rendered through the operator's existing embedded-chart,\n45\t  server-side-apply pattern.\n46\t- A CR configuration surface that enables the split-server artifact serving\n47\t  topology (exact field naming is an implementation decision for the team).\n48\t- Propagation of workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`,\n49\t  `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only\n50\t  instance using the same configuration mechanisms already used for the main\n51\t  tracking deployment.\n52\t- Conditional creation of the artifacts-only instance's Gateway API\n53\t  HTTPRoute based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's\n54\t  existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n55\t- kube-rbac-proxy sidecar deployed on the artifacts-only instance identically\n56\t  to the main tracking deployment (authentication layer unchanged).\n57\t- Operator validation that rejects configurations enabling split-server\n58\t  artifact serving where the artifacts-only instance would lack the workspace\n59\t  flags (misconfiguration could let artifact requests bypass workspace\n60\t  validation).\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, the operator\n65\t  reconciles the CR and creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment,\n66\t  Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment, measured\n67\t  by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the correct flag\n68\t  combinations.\n69\t- The artifacts-only Deployment runs with `--artifacts-only\n70\t  --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name\n71\t  kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`, measured by inspecting the container\n72\t  command in the rendered Deployment spec.\n73\t- The rendered flag combination is verified against the flag combination the\n74\t  workspace-aware artifacts-only server supports, and end-to-end artifact\n75\t  serving with workspace validation is verified against a server image\n76\t  carrying that capability (coordination point with the server-side work —\n77\t  not a start-order dependency).\n78\t- The operator rejects CRs that enable split-server artifact serving without\n79\t  the workspace configuration, with a clear validation error.\n80\t- CRs without split-server artifact serving configured reconcile exactly as\n81\t  before — no new resources are created and existing resources are unchanged\n82\t  (single-tenant and non-workspace deployments are unaffected).\n83\t- The artifacts-only HTTPRoute is created only when the Gateway API CRD is\n84\t  discovered at runtime, consistent with the operator's existing conditional\n85\t  pattern.\n86\t- The chart change adds new templates without structural changes to the chart\n87\t  architecture; if structural changes turn out to be required, the epic is\n88\t  re-split (see the decomposition summary's Health Warnings).\n89\t\n90\t## HLR Traceability\n91\t\n92\t- HLR-5 (P1): MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as\n93\t  a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute.\n94\t- HLR-4 (P0, constraining acceptance criterion): configurations without\n95\t  `--enable-workspaces` retain current behavior — the operator's share is a\n96\t  no-change constraint on the opt-in topology, not P0-enabling work.\n97\t\n98\t## Risks / Notes\n99\t\n100\t- A split-server topology adds operational surface (two Deployments, two\n101\t  Services, two HTTPRoutes); misconfiguration could let artifact requests\n102\t  bypass workspace validation. Mitigated by operator-level validation of the\n103\t  workspace flag combination.\n104\t- The strategy's architecture review and ODH/RHOAI build onboarding\n105\t  prerequisites are pending human review and cover this epic's design.\n106\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bca13937492c95c2","agent_id":"a4b202be07365c067","session_id":"c475d54c-6029-4a26-8892-bfb5b0182313","uuid":"d7001f8d-6fdf-4ff4-ae1b-2807210c9b31","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:39:14.255Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a101cc3d4d2009c3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
