{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91b70db337fd2be7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n3\ttitle: Decide the artifact traffic routing mechanism for the split-server topology\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Decide the artifact traffic routing mechanism for the split-server topology\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation decides how the MLflow operator should configure artifact\n30\ttraffic routing from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated\n31\tartifacts-only instance, and whether the tracking server needs a\n32\tconfiguration change to delegate artifact operations. The answer determines\n33\twhich downstream routing work exists: gateway-level routing only, or\n34\ttracking-server delegation requiring both operator configuration and\n35\tserver-side support. The outcome selects between two bounded conditional\n36\twork plans.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Evaluate routing artifact traffic to the dedicated instance at the\n41\t  gateway/HTTPRoute level (path-based routing on the artifacts-only\n42\t  instance's own Service and HTTPRoute, with no tracking server change).\n43\t- Evaluate routing via tracking-server delegation (the main tracking\n44\t  deployment configured to delegate artifact operations to the dedicated\n45\t  instance, requiring server-side configuration support).\n46\t- Analyze the tracking server's existing artifact proxy configuration\n47\t  surface and the operator's existing routing/rendering patterns to determine\n48\t  feasibility of each option.\n49\t- Assess the security implication either way: no routing path may allow\n50\t  artifact requests to bypass workspace validation.\n51\t- Record the bounded outcome decision: outcome A (gateway-level routing\n52\t  suffices — operator work only) or outcome B (tracking-server delegation\n53\t  required — operator plus server-side configuration work).\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- A documented recommendation identifying the routing mechanism, with a\n58\t  feasibility analysis grounded in the operator's rendering/routing code and\n59\t  the tracking server's artifact proxy configuration surface.\n60\t- An explicit determination of whether the tracking server requires a\n61\t  configuration change to delegate artifact operations, with the\n62\t  configuration surface it would use if so.\n63\t- An analysis confirming the selected mechanism cannot route artifact\n64\t  requests around workspace validation.\n65\t- The bounded outcome is recorded so the matching conditional work plan can\n66\t  be selected.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the\n71\t  dedicated artifacts-only instance — this investigation determines the\n72\t  mechanism and scope of that work.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bca13937492c95c2","agent_id":"a4b202be07365c067","session_id":"c475d54c-6029-4a26-8892-bfb5b0182313","uuid":"e9f1a1e5-c26a-4a19-9daf-c5d0039ef2df","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:39:15.078Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-91b70db337fd2be7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
