{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-876d8401dbedbc78","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n3\ttitle: Measure per-request latency overhead of workspace validation\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n11\tinvestigation_signals:\n12\t  question_specificity: 0\n13\t  source_accessibility: 1\n14\t  local_runnability: 0\n15\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n16\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n17\timplementation_type: null\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Low\n20\tai_implementability_score: -2\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Measure per-request latency overhead of workspace validation\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis investigation measures the latency overhead that per-request workspace\n31\tvalidation (workspace store lookup plus auth plugin validation) adds to\n32\tartifact serving, and produces a recommendation on whether short-TTL caching\n33\tof workspace membership decisions is required at launch or can be deferred\n34\tto a follow-up release. The strategy's performance NFR specifies no latency\n35\ttarget, so the measurement also supplies the factual basis for the\n36\tPM/Engineering threshold decision.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Define a measurement methodology for per-request overhead of the\n41\t  workspace-aware artifact serving path (workspace store lookup, workspace\n42\t  resolution, authorization delegation) against a representative\n43\t  Kubernetes-backed workspace store.\n44\t- Execute the measurement against the implemented workspace-aware\n45\t  artifacts-only serving capability (the measurement subject must exist\n46\t  first).\n47\t- Report the measured overhead distribution and compare it against the\n48\t  latency threshold PM/Engineering considers acceptable.\n49\t- Recommend: caching required at launch, or deferrable to a follow-up\n50\t  release — with the evidence that supports the recommendation.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- A measurement report stating the methodology, environment, and per-request\n55\t  latency overhead of workspace validation on the artifact serving path.\n56\t- A recorded recommendation (caching at launch vs. deferred) with supporting\n57\t  measurements, submitted for the PM/Engineering acceptability decision.\n58\t- If the overhead is within acceptable limits, the follow-on caching work is\n59\t  explicitly marked deferrable; if not, the caching work is confirmed as\n60\t  required for launch.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- Supports the Performance NFR attached to the P0 artifact-serving HLRs\n65\t  (HLR-1 through HLR-3): workspace resolution adds a store lookup and\n66\t  validation per artifact request; no latency target is specified in the RFE\n67\t  or architecture context.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bca13937492c95c2","agent_id":"a4b202be07365c067","session_id":"c475d54c-6029-4a26-8892-bfb5b0182313","uuid":"993e89ee-6470-49b9-8e45-bc8a3b4fe185","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:39:18.585Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-876d8401dbedbc78","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
