{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93e2ef3e2e7f127e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E006\n3\ttitle: Short-TTL caching of workspace membership decisions in artifact serving\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the latency measurement shows per-request overhead within\n16\t    acceptable limits, this epic is removed and caching is deferred to a follow-up\n17\t    release.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 3\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Short-TTL caching of workspace membership decisions in artifact serving\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tImplement short-TTL caching of workspace membership decisions in the\n40\tworkspace-aware artifact serving path, consistent with caching patterns\n41\talready used in the tracking server's auth path, to bound the per-request\n42\tlatency overhead of workspace validation. This epic is conditional: it is\n43\tremoved (and caching deferred to a follow-up release) if the latency\n44\tmeasurement shows the per-request overhead is within acceptable limits\n45\twithout it.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- A short-TTL cache of workspace membership decisions consulted by the\n50\t  artifact-request workspace validation path, following the caching patterns\n51\t  already used in the tracking server's auth path.\n52\t- Cache behavior that preserves the fail-closed security posture: a cache\n53\t  miss or unreachable workspace store still denies unvalidatable requests;\n54\t  cached decisions must not extend authorization beyond their TTL.\n55\t- Configuration of the cache TTL (exact mechanism is an implementation\n56\t  decision for the team).\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Workspace membership decisions are cached with a short TTL, and repeated\n61\t  artifact requests within the TTL avoid redundant workspace store lookups,\n62\t  demonstrated by measurement against the uncached baseline.\n63\t- Authorization behavior is unchanged by caching: member requests are served\n64\t  (HTTP 200), non-member requests are denied (HTTP 403), and the fail-closed\n65\t  behavior when the workspace store is unreachable is preserved (HTTP 503\n66\t  once cached decisions expire).\n67\t- Expired cache entries trigger re-validation rather than serving on stale\n68\t  authorization.\n69\t- Tests cover cache expiry, invalidation, and the fail-closed interaction.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- Supports the Performance NFR for the P0 artifact-serving HLRs (HLR-1\n74\t  through HLR-3); implements the strategy's risk mitigation for per-request\n75\t  workspace resolution overhead. Not an HLR itself — its necessity is decided\n76\t  by the latency measurement and PM/Engineering threshold decision.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bca13937492c95c2","agent_id":"a4b202be07365c067","session_id":"c475d54c-6029-4a26-8892-bfb5b0182313","uuid":"c88158cc-0492-4157-a028-5b6b1efcacf3","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:39:19.186Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-93e2ef3e2e7f127e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
