{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84ed40ca67fe410e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E007\n3\ttitle: Decide the telemetry channel for workspace access-denial audit events\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 0\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Decide the telemetry channel for workspace access-denial audit events\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's open question of whether\n30\tworkspace access denials in artifact serving should generate audit events\n31\tthrough server logs, OTLP telemetry, or the Kubernetes audit log. It is a\n32\tPM/Security decision informed by the platform's existing telemetry\n33\tinfrastructure; the answer determines the scope of the audit-logging\n34\timplementation work.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Enumerate the three candidate channels (server logs, OTLP, Kubernetes\n39\t  audit log) with the integration effort and operational characteristics of\n40\t  each for artifact-serving denial events.\n41\t- Gather PM/Security input on the required audit characteristics\n42\t  (retention, searchability, correlation with tenant identity).\n43\t- Record the decision and the scope it implies for the audit-logging\n44\t  implementation: the strategy's HLR defaults to server logs, so any other\n45\t  channel rewrites that work's scope.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- A recorded decision on the telemetry channel for workspace access-denial\n50\t  audit events, with rationale and the PM/Security owners' sign-off.\n51\t- A defined scope for the audit event content (which fields: user, workspace,\n52\t  artifact path, decision) and the selected channel's integration approach.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- HLR-8 (P2): audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving\n57\t  — this investigation determines the channel and therefore the scope of\n58\t  that work.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bca13937492c95c2","agent_id":"a4b202be07365c067","session_id":"c475d54c-6029-4a26-8892-bfb5b0182313","uuid":"d51271ae-3d45-4067-851b-33bdb6a5cf75","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:39:22.322Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-84ed40ca67fe410e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
