{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b16082d03c608ad6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E008\n3\ttitle: Audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E007\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E007\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the telemetry-channel decision selects OTLP or the Kubernetes\n16\t    audit log rather than server logs, this epic's implementation is rewritten to\n17\t    emit through the selected channel.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 2\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tImplement audit logging of workspace access denials in the workspace-aware\n40\tartifact serving path, so that denied artifact requests (HTTP 403 responses\n41\tand fail-closed denials) generate audit events through the telemetry channel\n42\tselected by the channel decision (server logs by default per the strategy's\n43\tHLR; OTLP or the Kubernetes audit log if so decided). This epic instruments\n44\tthe denial path built by the workspace-aware artifact serving work; it does\n45\tnot rebuild that path.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- Emit an audit event for each workspace access denial in artifact serving,\n50\t  capturing the user identity, workspace context, artifact path, and denial\n51\t  reason.\n52\t- Deliver events through the selected telemetry channel (server logs by\n53\t  default; the implementation is rewritten if the channel decision selects\n54\t  OTLP or the Kubernetes audit log).\n55\t- Ensure audit emission cannot fail open the serving path: a failure to emit\n56\t  an audit event must not cause a denied request to be served.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Every workspace access denial in artifact serving (HTTP 403 insufficient\n61\t  workspace permissions, and fail-closed unavailability denials) produces an\n62\t  audit event through the selected channel containing user, workspace,\n63\t  artifact path, and decision.\n64\t- Audit events are verifiably produced for the denial scenarios in the\n65\t  strategy's acceptance criteria (member of workspace A denied for workspace\n66\t  B; workspace store unreachable).\n67\t- Audit emission failures do not alter the denial decision (fail-closed\n68\t  behavior is independent of audit emission).\n69\t- Tests cover event content and emission for all denial paths.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-8 (P2): audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving\n74\t  through server logs (or the channel selected by the decision this epic is\n75\t  gated on).\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bca13937492c95c2","agent_id":"a4b202be07365c067","session_id":"c475d54c-6029-4a26-8892-bfb5b0182313","uuid":"74f54676-87e7-4764-b281-3fde8d116f96","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:39:23.127Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b16082d03c608ad6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
