{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7cbaf2c970dbd7b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-B-E009\n3\ttitle: Refactor plugin workspace resolution into an independent initialization path\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If verification shows workspace resolution is not coupled to\n16\t    tracking-store initialization, no refactor is needed and this epic is removed;\n17\t    verification-only work suffices.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 1\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 0\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 7\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Refactor plugin workspace resolution into an independent initialization path\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tConditional work plan for the outcome where the plugin-coupling investigation\n39\tfinds that `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` workspace resolution IS coupled to the\n40\ttracking server's full initialization path (tracking store, model registry\n41\tstore). Factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path\n42\twithin the plugin so it functions in the artifacts-only server context, then\n43\tverify correctness end to end. The plugin's existing interface is preserved.\n44\t\n45\t## Scope\n46\t\n47\t- Refactor the plugin's workspace resolution / workspace store initialization\n48\t  into an independent initialization path, decoupled from tracking store and\n49\t  model registry store availability, following the refactor plan produced by\n50\t  the investigation.\n51\t- Preserve the plugin's registration through the `mlflow.workspace_provider`\n52\t  entry point group and its loading via the workspace store registry, so the\n53\t  tracking server's existing workspace behavior is unchanged.\n54\t- Verification and tests (plugin-level and integration against a\n55\t  workspace-aware artifacts-only server instance) covering workspace member\n56\t  and non-member artifact requests.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Workspace resolution initializes in the artifacts-only server context\n61\t  without tracking store initialization, demonstrated by test evidence\n62\t  against the refactored initialization path.\n63\t- The tracking server's existing (non-artifact) workspace behavior is\n64\t  unchanged by the refactor — no regression in workspace resolution for\n65\t  tracking operations.\n66\t- Workspace resolution from artifact request paths produces correct\n67\t  authorization decisions: member requests allowed, non-member requests\n68\t  denied, consistent with the workspace-aware artifact serving behavior.\n69\t- Regression tests are merged covering workspace resolution in the\n70\t  artifacts-only context and the preserved tracking-server context.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- HLR-7 (P1, raised to P0 by inheritance): auth plugin workspace resolution\n75\t  functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store\n76\t  initialization.\n77\t- Co-enables HLR-2 (P0): end-to-end workspace-validated artifact serving.\n78\t\n79\t## Branch Condition\n80\t\n81\tSelected when the plugin-coupling investigation determines workspace\n82\tresolution is coupled to tracking store initialization. If that outcome does\n83\tnot hold (no coupling is found), this refactoring epic is removed —\n84\tverification-only work suffices.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bca13937492c95c2","agent_id":"a4b202be07365c067","se