n tracking\n53\t  deployment unchanged.\n54\t- Validation that the routing path cannot direct artifact requests around\n55\t  workspace validation.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Artifact requests are routed to the dedicated artifacts-only instance and\n60\t  non-artifact requests to the main tracking deployment, verified against a\n61\t  deployed split-server topology.\n62\t- Routing is configured declaratively by the operator from a single MLflow\n63\t  CR (users do not manage individual routing resources).\n64\t- No routing path allows artifact requests to bypass workspace validation.\n65\t- The main tracking deployment's configuration is unchanged apart from the\n66\t  routing of artifact traffic.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the\n71\t  dedicated artifacts-only instance — gateway-level mechanism.\n72\t\n73\t## Branch Condition\n74\t\n75\tSelected when the routing-mechanism investigation determines gateway-level\n76\trouting suffices. If that outcome does not hold (tracking-server delegation\n77\tis required), this epic is rewritten to the delegation-based approach of the\n78\talternative plan.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bca13937492c95c2","agent_id":"a4b202be07365c067","session_id":"c475d54c-6029-4a26-8892-bfb5b0182313","uuid":"c725875e-e6e1-4162-aafc-7adc12979c49","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:39:30.832Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b43c5a1812d387f1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
