on reference — verified\n51\t  by acceptance criteria, not a start-order dependency).\n52\t- Routing rules that keep non-artifact traffic on the main tracking\n53\t  deployment unchanged.\n54\t- Validation that the delegation path cannot direct artifact requests around\n55\t  workspace validation.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- The main tracking deployment's rendered configuration delegates artifact\n60\t  operations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, verified against a\n61\t  deployed split-server topology.\n62\t- The rendered delegation configuration matches the delegation surface the\n63\t  tracking server supports (coordination point with the server-side\n64\t  delegation work — not a start-order dependency).\n65\t- Artifact requests reach the dedicated instance and are workspace-validated\n66\t  there; non-artifact requests continue to be served by the main tracking\n67\t  deployment.\n68\t- No routing path allows artifact requests to bypass workspace validation.\n69\t- Routing is configured declaratively by the operator from a single MLflow\n70\t  CR.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the\n75\t  dedicated artifacts-only instance — tracking-server delegation mechanism.\n76\t\n77\t## Branch Condition\n78\t\n79\tSelected when the routing-mechanism investigation determines\n80\ttracking-server delegation is required. If that outcome does not hold\n81\t(gateway-level routing suffices), this epic is removed in favor of the\n82\tgateway-level routing plan.\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bca13937492c95c2","agent_id":"a4b202be07365c067","session_id":"c475d54c-6029-4a26-8892-bfb5b0182313","uuid":"6ecbe10f-fd70-49cc-a578-75697768649a","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:39:31.611Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-961bf1a80ab23dd9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re