rtifacts-only instance as the\n51\t  target for artifact operations.\n52\t- Behavior when the designation is absent: current artifact serving behavior\n53\t  is preserved (backwards compatibility).\n54\t- Tests for the delegation configuration surface.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- The tracking server can be configured to delegate artifact operations to a\n59\t  designated artifacts-only instance, and artifact requests are served\n60\t  through that instance when the configuration is present.\n61\t- With the configuration absent, the tracking server's artifact serving\n62\t  behavior is unchanged (no existing API contracts, CLI arguments, or\n63\t  configuration keys change meaning).\n64\t- The delegation configuration surface is documented for the operator to\n65\t  consume.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- Supports HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to\n70\t  the dedicated artifacts-only instance — server-side share of the\n71\t  delegation mechanism.\n72\t- HLR-4 (P0, constraining acceptance criterion): configurations without the\n73\t  delegation designation retain current behavior.\n74\t\n75\t## Branch Condition\n76\t\n77\tSelected when the routing-mechanism investigation determines the tracking\n78\tserver requires a configuration change to delegate artifact operations. If\n79\tthat outcome does not hold (gateway-level routing suffices), this server-side\n80\twork is removed — no delegation configuration is needed.\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bca13937492c95c2","agent_id":"a4b202be07365c067","session_id":"c475d54c-6029-4a26-8892-bfb5b0182313","uuid":"dcc2ecc5-8075-4e79-bf21-4b44fd086358","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:39:32.339Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad3f230a39355540","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
