{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b42f045bf0093e1a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-8009\n3\tscore: 14\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues: []\n7\terror: null\n8\t---\n9\t## Review Summary\n10\t\n11\tScore: 14/14 — pass\n12\tRecommendation: accept\n13\t\n14\tContract validator: OK (`validate_decomposition.py RHAISTRAT-8009` exits 0 — epic body\n15\tsections, canonical component names, Rule 11 docs-last coverage, priority inheritance,\n16\timplementation-type parallelism, and epic-size overage triggers all pass). Triage check:\n17\t`triage: null` (full decomposition), so the 8-epic main plan plus 5 conditional branch\n18\tepics is the expected shape. Reviewed: strategy, decomposition summary, 8 main-plan\n19\tepics, 5 branch epics, 13 ai-signals files, and the architecture context for mlflow and\n20\tmlflow-operator.\n21\t\n22\t## Criterion Details\n23\t\n24\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n25\tAll 8 HLRs map to at least one epic, and the traceability matrix in the summary is\n26\tcomplete and consistent with each epic's HLR Traceability section: HLR-1/2/3/4 → E002\n27\t(P0), HLR-2 additionally co-enabled by BRANCH-A/B-E009, HLR-5 → E003, HLR-6 →\n28\tBRANCH-A/B-E010 (+ BRANCH-B-E011), HLR-7 → BRANCH-A/B-E009, HLR-8 → E008. Priority\n29\tinheritance is correct throughout: E001 (P0) gates the plugin branch epics that\n30\tco-enable P0 HLR-2, and those branch epics are correctly raised to P0; no lower-priority\n31\tepic blocks P0 work (E003, E004 gate only P1 work; E005, E007 gate only P2 work). The\n32\tstrategy-internal priority inversion on HLR-7 (labeled P1 but required for P0 HLR-2's\n33\tend-to-end acceptance) is correctly surfaced as Health Warning 1 rather than silently\n34\tinherited or ignored. HLR-4's operator share is carried as a constraining no-change AC\n35\ton E003 while E002 (P0) carries the P0 capability — a documented, correct resolution,\n36\tnot priority colla